PURPOSE Branch on original vehicle/package arc incidences and propagate each
    decision to both the inherited route pool and all future pricing models.
REFERENCES Paper branch-and-bound-style integrality framework;
    Program.Generating_new_node, BB_node, BB_info.
ASSUMPTIONS The paper leaves the branch rule unspecified. The rule below
    branches on the arc marginal closest to 0.5, using stable keys and deterministic
    tie breaking. Fractional nodes without an admissible arc remain unresolved.
INPUT parent node, split route pool, current LP weights, immutable network catalog.
OUTPUT two child nodes or an explicit no-candidate/key-contract outcome.

TYPE ArcBranchDecision
    ownerKind in {vehicle,package}; ownerId; catalogSignature
    originalArcRecordId; complete tail/head point identities and times
    value in {0,1}
    # Preserve record identity if multiple arcs have the same endpoints.

PROCEDURE SelectLegacyBranch(pool,weights,network,config,node=none)
    marginals := ReconstructArcMarginals(pool,weights).
    candidates := every owner/arc marginal satisfying
        integralityTolerance < marginal < 1-integralityTolerance.
    Remove any decision already fixed by node.inheritedDecisions, if node exists.
    IF candidates is empty: RETURN no_candidate.
    Choose the marginal closest to 0.5; break ties by kind, owner and arc ID.
    Require the key to resolve to one original record in this catalog.
    IF resolution fails: RETURN branch_key_failure.
    RETURN ArcBranchDecision without child value.

PROCEDURE ColumnAllowed(route,node)
    FOR each decision whose owner matches route
        usesArc := route's incidence for decision.originalArcRecordId.
        IF usesArc != decision.value: RETURN false.
    IF route is a paired-fragment package route
        Check decisions on both fragments under their parent package identity.
    RETURN true.

PROCEDURE GenerateChildren(parent,decision)
    IF decision is absent or invalid: RETURN branch_unresolved.
    FOR childValue IN [0,1]
        child := independent copy of parent restrictions and complete route pool.
        Assign fresh node id, parent id and depth=parent.depth+1.
        Add decision with childValue to child.inheritedDecisions and to the
            matching vehicleBranches/packageBranches collection.
        Reject contradictory decisions on the same original arc record.
        Keep only routes satisfying ColumnAllowed(route,child).
        Remove both stored fragments whenever their complete package q is removed.
        Update costs, coverage, ownership, incidence and transposed dictionaries.
        Set child.status=active; clear stale master duals and solve results.
        Retain immutable catalog identity; recalculate child pool/branch signatures.
        Do not infer full-model infeasibility merely because a filtered pool is empty.
    RETURN zeroChild,oneChild.

PROCEDURE ApplyBranchesToPricing(owner,arcVariables,node)
    FOR every decision for owner
        Resolve its original record in this pricing catalog.
        IF decision.value=1 AND record absent: RETURN infeasible_branch_model.
        IF record absent AND decision.value=0: CONTINUE.
        Add arcVariables[record] = decision.value.
    RETURN applied.
    # Vehicle pricing applies vehicle decisions; target-package pricing applies
    # package decisions. Optional supporting-vehicle solves apply both through
    # their fixed package path and vehicle constraints.

TERMINATION
    The two children partition the current owner's binary arc decision.
    If LP weights remain fractional but no supported arc branch exists, retain
        branch_unresolved. A valid integer-pool incumbent may still be reported.
    Preserve unresolved nodes. Restricted-master objectives cannot justify pruning.
    Report the explored scope and incumbent; full-model optimality remains unproven.
